BEGIN_PGML Graphs that are connected and contain no cycles are called trees. For each graph, how many edges must you remove to turn it into a tree? (If it is already a tree, the answer would be 0.)
[`G_1\text{:}`] [_]{6}{5}; [`G_2\text{:}`] [_]{2}{5}; [`G_3\text{:}`] [_]{2}{5}; [`G_4\text{:}`] [_]{0}{5}.
